  "reasoning_content": "We need answer user: \"Explain how a relational database executes a SQL query, from parsing and planning through indexing, joins, transactions, and returning rows. Write a detailed technical tutorial with concrete examples and tradeoffs, including common performance pitfalls. Use complete sentences and avoid repeating yourself.\"\n\nNeed produce detailed technical tutorial. Need final only. Need be thorough, complete sentences, avoid repetition. Need cover parsing, planning, indexing, joins, transactions, returning rows. Concrete examples and tradeoffs, common performance pitfalls.\n\nNeed structure. Could use headings. Need ensure complete sentences. Avoid repeating. Let's plan.\n\nTitle: How a relational database executes a SQL query.\n\nSections:\n1. High-level pipeline: client sends SQL, server parses, validates, optimizes, executes, returns.\n2. Parsing and validation: lexical analysis, syntax tree, semantic analysis, name resolution, type checking, privilege checks. Example SELECT with ambiguous column, missing table. Tradeoffs: strict vs permissive, prepared statements.\n3. Query rewriting and normalization: view expansion, common subexpression, predicate pushdown, constant folding. Example WHERE 1=1, IN list.\n4. Optimization/planning: logical plan, physical plan, cost model, statistics, cardinality estimates, access paths. Explain plan. Example:\nCREATE TABLE customers (id INT PRIMARY KEY, city TEXT, status TEXT);\nCREATE INDEX idx_customers_city ON customers(city);\nSELECT * FROM customers WHERE city='Berlin' AND status='active';\nOptimizer chooses index scan vs seq scan. Cost: rows, pages, CPU, I/O. Selectivity. Tradeoffs: index maintenance, memory, stale stats.\n5. Indexes: B-tree, hash, GIN/GiST, covering, composite, partial, expression. How used: point lookup, range, sort, join. Example composite index (city,status) vs (status,city). Tradeoffs: write amplification, index bloat, selectivity, index-only scans. Pitfalls: leading wildcard LIKE '%x', functions on indexed column, implicit type casts, low selectivity, over-indexing, index-only scan visibility map.\n6. Execution engine: Volcano/pull model, operators: SeqScan, IndexScan, Filter, Sort, HashJoin, NestedLoop, Aggregate, Limit. Example plan.\n7. Joins: nested loop, hash join, merge join. Example:\nSELECT o.id, c.name FROM orders o JOIN customers c ON",
